2026-10-08  Barak A. Pearlmutter  <barak@pearlmutter.net>

	* swisswatch.c: add --tz=ZONE option, after buici-clock.  The time is
	taken from a GTimeZone for ZONE, and the zone name is drawn on the
	face above the centre, beneath the hands (draw_label, label_fit).
	The label is shrunk to stay inside the marks, broken after its last
	'/' when that lets it be larger, and haloed in the face colour so
	marks it crosses are knocked out.  Each face sets its own label font,
	colour, size and position.  The window title includes the zone.
	(update_time): use the GTimeZone offset when --tz is given.

	* swisswatch.c: draw the bezel from new FaceConfig fields instead of
	as a circle mark, with the same stroke width as the hour marks (as
	in buici-clock), wholly inside the face so a shaped window no longer
	clips half of it.  apply_face shrinks the dial contents (dial_scale)
	so the marks clear the bezel.  Thicken the swisswatch bezel to match
	its hour marks, and darken it.

	* swisswatch.h2m, README.md: document --tz.

